-did-not-meet-prong-one-under-either-provision-of-the-dna-act)1097 0 R(the-criminal-court-erred-in-denying-mr-carruthers-dna-motion)1096 0 R(the-criminal-courts-conclusion-that-mr-carruthers-has-not-established-that-his-motion-was-not-filed-for-purposes-of-delay-is-not-supported-by-substantial-evidence)1101 0 R(the-criminal-courts-denial-of-the-motion-to-compel-unconstitutionally-deprived-mr-carruthers-of-his-right-to-dna-testing)1104 0 R(the-criminal-courts-denial-of-the-motion-to-compel-violated-mr-carruthers-right-to-due-process)1102 0 R(the-criminal-courts-denial-of-the-motion-to-compel-was-without-adequate-procedure)1105 0 R(the-criminal-courts-dna-order-relied-on-undisputedly-false-information)1098 0 R(the-medical-examiner-disavowed-his-testimony-that-the-victims-were-buried-alive)1084 0 R(the-requested-dna-testing-could-confirm-mr-carruthers-innocence-andor-inculpate-an-alternative-suspect)1088 0 R(this-court-has-jurisdiction-and-should-review-the-compel-order-as-an-extraordinary-appeal-under-tennessee-rule-of-appellate-procedure-10)1103 0 R]>>>>>>
